# Deploy Key — Private Repo Access
# ===================================
# This file is a placeholder. The actual deploy key is managed via the
# Coolify UI and stored in the coolify-data Docker volume.
#
# Setup steps:
#
# 1. Generate a key pair (if you don't have one):
#      ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "coolify-deploy@tp-gen" -f ./id_ed25519 -N ""
#
# 2. Add the PUBLIC key to GitHub:
#      Repo → Settings → Deploy keys → Add deploy key
#      Title: coolify-tp-gen  |  Key: contents of id_ed25519.pub  |  Allow write: no
#
# 3. Add the PRIVATE key to Coolify:
#      Coolify UI → Keys & Tokens → SSH Keys → Add SSH Key
#      Paste contents of id_ed25519 (private key)
#
# 4. When creating the GitHub source in Coolify, select this SSH key.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit the actual private key to this repository.
